.TH "HEE\-MAIL" "8" "" "" "HEE Tools"
.SH NAME
hee\-mail \- mailboxes, aliases and master access on the fleet\[aq]s
mail exchanger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
hee mail list
hee mail add     NAME[\[at]DOMAIN] \-recipients KEYID[,KEYID...]
hee mail passwd  NAME[\[at]DOMAIN] \-recipients KEYID[,KEYID...]
hee mail alias   ADDR TARGET
hee mail unalias ADDR
hee mail master  NAME[\[at]DOMAIN]
hee mail unmaster NAME[\[at]DOMAIN]
hee mail record  [\-write]
hee mail check   [DOMAIN]
hee mail domain  list | add DOMAIN | handoff DOMAIN
hee mail login   NAME[\[at]DOMAIN]
hee mail help
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IP
.EX
One mailbox is three things that must agree: a row in the mail host\[aq]s
virtual table (where the address goes), a credential in two files on that
host (smtpd for submission, dovecot for IMAP), and a sealed password
someone can actually open. This tool keeps them in step; doing it by hand
is how a password works on 587 and not on 993.

The mail host is named by a package directory \-\- the fleet\-ops
hosts/<mx>/ tree that carries droplet.conf (its address), known_hosts
(its pinned key) and tables/ (its domains and virtuals). Default:
\[ti]/git/fleet\-ops/hosts/mx1\-tcosagent\-com, or $HEE_MAIL_PKG.

add generates a password with hee\-pwgen, seals it to \-recipients as
mail\-<name> in the package repo\[aq]s .hee/secrets, hashes it ON the mail
host with \[ga]smtpctl encrypt\[ga], writes that hash to both credential files,
and creates the Maildir owned by vmail. The plaintext is held in one
shell variable, handed to gpg and to ssh on stdin, and never printed,
never in argv, never in a file. passwd is the same thing for an address
that already exists \-\- a rotation.

Seal to every key that has a real reason to open it: the mailbox owner\[aq]s
personal key AND the per\-host key of each machine they read mail from
(HEE_POLICY §24). A password sealed only to a key that lives on another
machine is a password nobody can use where they are.

master makes an account a dovecot master user: it then opens any mailbox
as \[dq]<mailbox>*<master>\[dq] with its own password, and dovecot logs every
such login. No password is generated or changed, and nothing is copied.
This is how an operator reads the fleet\[aq]s mail without holding anyone
else\[aq]s credential.

record renders the mailbox list as YAML under the package\[aq]s repo
(mail/accounts.<domain>.yaml). It holds addresses, kinds and recipients
\-\- never a password or a hash. inv.lab already syncs fleet\-ops, so the
record is how mail identities reach the inventory rather than a second
API to keep alive.

domain add takes a zone this exchanger should receive for: a line in
tables/domains, a catch\-all row in tables/virtuals, and a records file
under the repo\[aq]s dns/ carrying MX, SPF, DKIM and DMARC for it. Nothing is
published \-\- bin/dns\-records.sh does that, per zone, and bin/push.sh
deploys the tables. One shared DKIM key signs every domain, because
filter\-dkimsign takes one key and many domains.

domain handoff is for selling. A domain is worth more with its mail
working, and a buyer must not receive the key that signs everyone else\[aq]s:
it prints the zone\[aq]s records, its addresses, and the exact steps to cut it
over \-\- starting with a FRESH per\-domain DKIM key, because the shared one
can never leave this fleet. Operator, 2026\-09\-19: \[dq]once we (if we) sell a
domain and it\[aq]s mail it should be fully configured to hand off. we build
businesses to sell, that is our deal.\[dq]

login is for the human at the keyboard: it opens that mailbox\[aq]s sealed
password, puts it on the clipboard, and prints the server settings to type
into a mail client. The password is never printed, never written to a
file, and never passed on a command line \-\- it goes from gpg into the
clipboard tool\[aq]s stdin and nowhere else. Clear the clipboard afterwards;
the tool says how.
.EE
.SH OPTIONS
.IP
.EX
\-recipients IDS   with add/passwd: GPG key ids or emails, comma separated
\-pkg DIR          the mail host package (default: $HEE_MAIL_PKG, else
                  \[ti]/git/fleet\-ops/hosts/mx1\-tcosagent\-com)
\-target root\[at]HOST override the address in the package\[aq]s droplet.conf
\-domain DOMAIN    default domain for a bare NAME (default: tcosagent.com)
\-write            with record: write the file (default prints it)
\-dry\-run          with add/passwd: run every check, change nothing
.EE
